@ddd

Purpose:
  Domain Driven Design references.

Use this index before introducing DDD concepts.

Owns: references\ddd\index.sdd
Concepts:
  @ddd.entity
      Identity-based domain object.

  @ddd.value-object
      Immutable value without identity.

  @ddd.aggregate
      Consistency boundary.

  @ddd.aggregate-root
      Entry point to aggregate.

  @ddd.repository
      Aggregate persistence abstraction.

  @ddd.domain-service
      Domain operation that does not naturally belong to an entity/value object.

  @ddd.domain-event
      Event representing a domain fact.

  @ddd.bounded-context
      Explicit domain model boundary.

DecisionGuide:
  Need identity?
    → @ddd.entity

  Need immutable value?
    → @ddd.value-object

  Need transaction/consistency boundary?
    → @ddd.aggregate

  Need persistence abstraction?
    → @ddd.repository

  Need domain operation without natural owner?
    → @ddd.domain-service

  Need business fact/event?
    → @ddd.domain-event

  Need separate model/language boundary?
    → @ddd.bounded-context

SuitableProjectTypes:
  GoodCandidates:
    @project.payment
    @project.order-management
    @project.core-banking

  UsuallyUnnecessary:
    @project.simple-crud
    @project.admin-panel

LayerMapping:
  L0: strategic/domain decisions
  L1: bounded contexts
  L2: aggregates/entities/value objects
  L3: application/domain services
  L4: infrastructure implementation

RelatedReferences:
  @architecture.layered
  @architecture.hexagonal
  @architecture.clean
  @patterns.repository

State: +
